<%# ============================================================================
    THE EPISTEMIC CHIP (#9) -- a proof's claim layer, marked unverified.

    ONE partial, because the chip appears on TWO surfaces: the Jev answer cards
    and the proof findings rows. A second, hand-tuned pill at either site is
    exactly the drift the #93 chip family exists to prevent, so both read this.

    It is a SIBLING of the dashed `.chip.miss` convention rather than a member
    of it: `.miss` means "intentionally empty", and a flag is not an absence.
    It is a claim about the data, so it takes a MEANING band like `.badge.warn`
    does -- needs_factcheck is the amber "unchecked" and disputed the red
    "readings disagree" -- reusing the #93 vocabulary instead of inventing a
    colour. One rule, two names (`.chip` and `.badge`), the way the semantic
    layer already spells it.

    Locals:
      flags  the proof's flags, as symbols -- `validation.epistemic_flags`.
             Renders NOTHING when empty: a proof nobody flagged carries no chip,
             and a row of empty pills is chrome, not information.
   ============================================================================ %>
<% Array(flags).map(&:to_sym).each do |flag| %>
  <% label = Validation::EPISTEMIC_FLAGS[flag] %>
  <% next unless label %>
  <span class="chip <%= flag %>"
        title="This proof's findings or Jev answers are unverified: <%= label %>."><%= label %></span>
<% end %>
